  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "W1-001",
      "severity": "medium",
      "items": [
        "D-117",
        "D-129",
        "D-132",
        "D-135",
        "D-173"
      ],
      "claim": "The \"Carried from earlier waves\" note narrows D-117/D-129 from \"every request that reaches the dispatcher\" to \"every request for which a Request is built\" and classes the dispatcher-level rejections (unsupported-method 501 of D-395, raw path not starting with /, path-validator 400) as outside middleware and onError. In the merged wave 3 code these are answered inside Dispatcher.handle/preCheck, i.e. they do reach the dispatcher, and D-400 exempts only TinyHttpd transport-level rejections from onError, standard error JSON and access log; D-422 (later wave) requires the dispatcher 501 to carry an access-log line. The note is silent on access log and requestId for these requests while note 4 gives 501 the standard error body, so an implementer following the note may drop middleware/onError/access-log coverage the frozen items require, or skip the access-log line and requestId.",
      "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-4/design.md:121; NaruServe-api/src/main/java/com/snoworca/naruserve/internal/Dispatcher.java:44-91; docs/research/naruserve-v1/design/00.design.md:230,245,304,381,382",
      "suggested_fix": "Reword the carried note: dispatcher-level rejections (501 unsupported method, 400 path checks) still get one access-log line and a standard error body whose requestId matches the log (D-132, D-135, D-173, D-422); state explicitly (and record in docs/api/middleware.md as the #5 decision) whether middleware and onError run for them, citing that no Request can carry an unrecognised method token, instead of silently restricting D-117/D-129."
    }
  ]
